            <ArticleTitle>The learning curve for transradial procedures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A14-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The learning curve for transradial procedure represents a major limitation for the widespread use of the technique. The rate of procedural failure can be as high as 10-16% during the first 30 or 40 cases. With appropriate training, persistence, and attention to the selection of patients and devices, most interventionalists manage to gain confidence after the first 100-200 cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
